BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Title: Negotiate from a written walk-away list) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Action: Enter the meeting with your perfect-deal terms and your deal breakers written down. Then trade on minimum) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (guarantees, term, territory, and enforcement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (Detail: Having goals and walk-away terms in hand gives you posture and keeps you professional and unemotional) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (across the negotiation [J.D. Houvener / Bold Patents Law Firm - ZbJhX8I0koA @ 00:02:26]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (Key's street method is to spend almost nothing until a company says yes. For the Michael Jordan Wall Ball, Key made) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (the prototype at Kinko's using a $15 Ohio Art backboard and a $10 poster, roughly $25 total. Key had a licensing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (agreement three days later, and the product earned about $100,000 in first-year royalties and sold for 10 years) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm ([gxeuCPaGeHY @ 00:04:08]. The Sweet Darts arrow needed no prototype and no intellectual property filing at all. It) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (paid about $10,000 for one Valentine's season and never sold again [Se-TzTVqhfY @ 00:02:53]. Brian Walker built) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (the original Light Chaser in three hours from parts already sitting in the shop. Walker assumed the $5,000 advance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (would be the only money ever seen. Instead the toy reached an estimated seven to eight hundred million dollars at retail) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (across more than a hundred versions [WEVVJ111b8o @ 00:04:13]. Key's current cost stack is even lower. An AI) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (prototype costs nothing, and 3D printing lets you Frankenstein a model together. Key uses AI to write a provisional) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (patent application and file it at the USPTO for $65 [hM7gpPqIDoQ @ 00:17:40]. The workhorse tool is the sell sheet, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (one-page advertisement that sells the benefit. Key uses it to gauge company interest before any real money moves on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (prototypes or patents.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (In the negotiation room, Sef Chang refuses to name a percentage first. Chang asks only whether the company is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (interested. The company then calls manufacturers, gets quotes, and crunches its own profit. Next Chang asks for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (cost rundown and moves the needle back and forth. If the percentage lands low, Chang negotiates for something else) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (that compensates [bO09tLv7ysM @ 00:01:06]. Krauss names those other levers. If the company offers three but you) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (wanted four, push the minimum guarantees higher. Require guaranteed sales figures with the rights coming back if they) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (are missed, or have the company pay for your patents [5pNsi_2H-J4 @ 00:03:20]. Houvener tells inventors to walk in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (with two plans: the perfect deal and the walk-away terms, such as at least four percent royalty or an exclusive grant.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (Holding those terms in hand gives you posture and keeps you professional instead of emotional [ZbJhX8I0koA @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (00:02:26]. Schell offers a trade most rookies miss. Under an exclusive arrangement, accept slightly lower royalties in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (exchange for putting the expensive obligation to enforce the patent on the licensee [cfPpWt8cw64 @ 00:02:52].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (Houvener also carves deals surgically. One option is licensing claims one through ten to one party and claims eleven) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (through twenty to another. Another is splitting make and sell rights across Canada, the US, and Mexico.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (The unit math is simple and brutal. Key's chart starts with the number of stores the licensee is in. Assume each store) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (sells one unit a week, because anything slower gets kicked to the curb. Then run the result at 3, 4, 5, and 6% across) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (chains like Walmart, Target, Lowe's, and Home Depot [5pNsi_2H-J4 @ 00:02:17]. Krauss contrasts the do-it-yourself) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (alternative. You could sell 5,000 to 20,000 units yourself at a 20% profit margin while working 60 to 80 hour weeks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (Or a licensee could move half a million units a year while you do no work [5pNsi_2H-J4 @ 00:04:09]. At the top end,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (Key's rotating label paid royalties for over 15 years and made about $10 million. It ran on Nescafe, Jim Beam, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (Lawry's, with sublicenses in Japan and Ireland [hM7gpPqIDoQ @ 00:13:06]. Walker's Light Chaser checks climbed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm (from $75,000 to $180,000, $260,000, and $340,000 in the breakout year. Later checks reached $250,000 to $350,000) Tj ET
