BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (for every foreign country, and reach around $500K by years 7 to 8 [ZzczaFujs3A @ 00:19:10]. That spend is why) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (offices treat patent-cost reimbursement as non-negotiable when a startup licensee signs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (Deal structure follows a standard sequence. At MIT, an option agreement comes first, and exercising it requires a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (business plan. Consideration then stacks several pieces: a license fee, equity for startups only as deferred compensation,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (maintenance fees, a sublicensing share, milestone payments such as FDA approval, royalties and patent-cost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (reimbursement [2ADE7tP4bYM @ 00:59:59]. Incoming money takes a 15% admin fee first and then recovers patent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (costs. Inventors as a pool then take one-third, while departments, labs, centers and the General Fund take two-thirds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm ([2ADE7tP4bYM @ 00:10:33]. Before any of that, faculty founder Bulovi? describes how MIT pays patent costs up) Tj ET
