BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (Norton, Rick Friedman and Nakisha Holder says terms are back-loaded as risk sharing and trade against each other, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (more upfront cash or equity can mean a lower royalty. Their worked anti-dilution example is 4%, or 400,000 shares,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (protected through a $2M raise, which investors accept if it is cleared at the first priced round. Past patent costs above) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm ($100K get scheduled across two years, with acceleration on financing [Q3YzwCiT2M4 @ 00:48:58].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (Pricing and marketing are where operators earn their keep. Columbia runs 35 PhD fellows on about 100 marketing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (campaigns a year. Herschwitz prices from benchmark databases, moves to a term sheet, and only then brings in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (attorneys. The 18-page boilerplate allows royalties that step down from 5% to 1%, plus caps, minimums and buyouts,) Tj ET
