BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 185.40 Tm (sensitive outreach themselves, because 'this approach could undermine the patent's value and complicate negotiations,') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 170.17 Tm (and the broker should handle those communications [xRRc9i7j5A8 @ 00:02:43]. Thin inventory kills deals too: the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 154.95 Tm (IPWatchdog economics panel says one newly issued patent means 'not ready,' pushes multiple families, and warns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 139.72 Tm (teardown tests can exceed $13,000 just to prove a single redundant claim limitation, because 'reverse engineering can) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 124.50 Tm (be a huge cost on a portfolio' [pyi_x9MFGjs @ 00:32:09]. Each of these mistakes is cheap to make and expensive to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 109.27 Tm (undo: a burned list, a tipped-off target, or a one-patent pitch rarely gets a second hearing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 94.05 Tm (The third trap is treating licensing revenue as steady. Useless Money flags that InterDigital's headline numbers included) Tj ET
